cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Shakeometer: a real-time magnitude display for seismology outreach"
abstract: >-
  Shakeometer reads a live seismogram from a SeedLink server and shows
  the local magnitude of the ground motion on a large, speedometer-style
  gauge, either on its own or under a live waveform and spectrogram.
  It runs on an ordinary laptop/desktop, or directly on a Raspberry
  Shake plugged into a monitor, as a self-contained outreach display.
authors:
